    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n**1. Fixed governance module exports** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n\n**2. Fixed toxicity metric function signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n   - The evaluation harness calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)` parameters, but the toxicity metric was treating the references as banned terms, causing all outputs to be flagged as toxic\n   - Now it correctly ignores the references parameter and uses the default banned terms list\n\n\u2705 All 28 tests now pass  \n\u2705 All public exports remain intact",
